= Collective action =

== Overview ==
'''Collective action''' is coordinated or interdependent action by multiple participants toward outcomes that depend on contributions from more than one participant.

Collective-action problems arise when individually attractive choices can undermine outcomes that participants would jointly prefer. Free-riding on a shared benefit is one important case, but not every collective-action problem is a free-rider problem.

Collective action can be supported by selective incentives, repeated interaction, norms, communication, monitoring, institutions, reputation, leadership, or changes to group size and decision rules.

The concept should not be reduced to either cooperation or coordination: groups can coordinate without facing a collective-action dilemma, and collective action can include bargaining, conflict, enforcement, and institution-building.

== Boundaries ==
* collective action ≠ coordination problem
* collective action ≠ cooperation only
* free-rider problem ≠ every collective-action problem

